WEBVTT

00:13.540 --> 00:18.460
I can do without something nuts like summer.
Well, I do want Natsukawa to be here, but...

00:22.880 --> 00:24.080
Whoa!

00:26.000 --> 00:27.630
So cool...

00:28.790 --> 00:31.460
The bliss of a classroom having air conditioning.

00:32.380 --> 00:35.420
Sleep tight, dear sweat glands.

00:35.420 --> 00:37.460
Morning, Sajotchi!

00:37.460 --> 00:38.040
Huh?

00:38.420 --> 00:39.250
Whoa...

00:39.790 --> 00:40.540
What?

00:41.000 --> 00:45.380
Could you not appear right in front of me
in scanty clothing? It's bad for my heart.

00:45.750 --> 00:46.500
Huh?

00:47.670 --> 00:50.580
Could you not call the summer uniform, scanty clothing?

00:50.710 --> 00:51.420
You perv.

00:51.830 --> 00:56.500
Well, but my defense power of about
95 went suddenly to 20, you know?

00:56.500 --> 00:57.670
Huh!?

00:58.080 --> 01:01.710
More importantly, are you okay with not gazing
upon a certain someone's summer uniform?

01:01.710 --> 01:02.630
Oh!

01:02.920 --> 01:04.750
Natsukawa's summer uniform look!

01:05.750 --> 01:07.750
It's a frolic of fairies.

01:07.750 --> 01:08.960
Wow. Creepy.

01:09.460 --> 01:12.960
Speaking of, Ashida, did you go to
Natsukawa's house on the weekend?

01:14.250 --> 01:17.170
Wanna know? Wanna hear about it?

01:17.170 --> 01:18.960
C'mon, don't leave me hanging like that.

01:20.460 --> 01:21.380
Good morning.

01:21.380 --> 01:21.960
Oh!

01:22.170 --> 01:23.790
Good morning!

01:24.080 --> 01:27.130
I'm starting homeroom. Get to your seats!

01:35.330 --> 01:35.960
Oh!

01:55.170 --> 01:58.960
<b>The Dreaming Boy</b>

01:55.170 --> 01:58.960
<b>is a Realist</b>

01:59.080 --> 02:04.670
With a command from the sky that's peeking out,
we hold onto our feelings as we depart

02:04.670 --> 02:09.380
Even though our eyes meet,
we're swayed by the wind into a roundabout way

02:10.460 --> 02:15.920
A dream snapshot taken by the blink of the eyes;
the memories adorn my heart

02:15.920 --> 02:21.330
It seems I like these times; even though they're frustrating

02:22.380 --> 02:27.290
Staying away then getting closer; a dream I'd started to give up on

02:27.540 --> 02:32.960
The day I can land that well; I want to try chasing after that

02:32.960 --> 02:38.380
The sky is filled up with the things that can't be all conveyed

02:38.540 --> 02:44.170
For some reason, the change in countenance
of your true feelings was at odds

02:44.170 --> 02:52.460
Even though I might get lost, the sky always had two heartbeats

02:52.460 --> 02:54.960
I've told you many times

02:55.130 --> 03:01.130
If these youthful feelings are joined together,
I wonder what kind of view will spread out

03:01.130 --> 03:05.790
I want to know that colorful feeling

03:12.580 --> 03:15.710
<b>Could You Not Call the Summer Uniform, Scanty Clothing?</b>

03:14.330 --> 03:15.710
That's all for today!

03:16.250 --> 03:17.920
Hey, Sajotchi!

03:17.920 --> 03:18.580
What?

03:19.000 --> 03:22.750
What's wrong? You still haven't even said
one word to Aichi today, you know?

03:22.750 --> 03:25.580
What? Well, you know, there is the distance factor.

03:25.880 --> 03:27.250
This is just normal, you know?

03:27.250 --> 03:27.830
Okay...

03:27.830 --> 03:28.500
Natsukawa.

03:28.380 --> 03:31.750
Plus, Natsukawa's being spoken to like that often now.

03:28.500 --> 03:29.170
Yeah?

03:29.330 --> 03:30.630
Thanks for the other day.

03:30.630 --> 03:31.750
Oh, yeah.

03:32.170 --> 03:33.830
And it'd be bad if I got in the way.

03:33.830 --> 03:36.710
"Got in the way"? And you're okay with that?

03:36.710 --> 03:41.960
Yeah. If I interact with her like before,
then I might destroy that environment, you know?

03:42.330 --> 03:43.420
That's not...

03:43.420 --> 03:46.670
For me to do things this way for now
will be good for Natsukawa.

03:48.130 --> 03:49.630
I don't know about that.

03:49.630 --> 03:50.330
Plus...

03:50.330 --> 03:50.750
Huh?

03:50.920 --> 03:53.670
If I get close to her, then I can't see the whole
perspective of "Summer Uniform Natsukawa!"   

03:53.670 --> 03:54.880
You perv!

03:55.710 --> 03:56.670
She's really cute.

03:56.670 --> 03:57.580
Stop that!

03:57.580 --> 03:58.460
A total pervert!

03:58.460 --> 03:59.170
What's up with that!?

03:59.170 --> 04:00.880
Lecher! You are a perv!

03:59.750 --> 04:00.330
Ow!

04:08.380 --> 04:09.380
Sajo.

04:09.750 --> 04:10.540
Nice job.  

04:10.540 --> 04:13.710
Hey. The soccer club is playing outstandingly.

04:13.710 --> 04:14.630
Well, yeah.

04:15.210 --> 04:17.540
Are you and Yamazaki still goofing off, these days?

04:17.830 --> 04:20.210
Don't lump me together with him.

04:20.330 --> 04:21.960
Poor Yamazaki.

04:22.420 --> 04:25.210
More importantly, you know, Airi-chan was cute.

04:25.380 --> 04:26.210
What's that?

04:28.130 --> 04:31.040
Natsukawa's little sister, huh? She's an angel.

04:31.420 --> 04:33.750
Just as I'd expect from someone
who's an actual big brother himself.

04:34.040 --> 04:34.960
Well, yeah.

04:35.580 --> 04:37.750
But Sajo, why didn't you come?

04:38.080 --> 04:40.500
I wasn't invited, so it's not like I had a choice.

04:40.670 --> 04:41.500
<b>Share 2 photos</b>

04:40.880 --> 04:43.170
Alright. I'm gonna tell on you to Yuki-chan.

04:43.170 --> 04:46.250
Oh! You idiot! Don't! Anything but that! Don't save it!

04:46.710 --> 04:47.460
Here ya go.

04:48.540 --> 04:51.960
Sasaki, you've misjudged your own little sister's
excessive attachment style to her brother.

04:52.210 --> 04:56.380
She personally requested to me that
I make a detailed report of your activities.

04:56.710 --> 04:58.130
And... Sent!

04:58.130 --> 04:59.040
Oh no!

04:59.710 --> 05:02.500
It's cute, you know? To love her big brother like that.

05:02.500 --> 05:03.290
That was quick!

05:03.290 --> 05:07.290
<b>Thank you very much for the photos.</b>

05:03.290 --> 05:07.290
<b>I will also become a little girl.</b>

05:03.670 --> 05:07.290
"Thank you very much for the photos.
I will also become a little girl."

05:07.670 --> 05:11.920
"I will become a little girl."?
Yuki-chan is a middle schooler, right?

05:12.040 --> 05:15.080
<b>Thank you very much for the photos.</b>

05:12.040 --> 05:15.080
<b>I will also become a little girl.</b>

05:12.040 --> 05:15.080
<b>If anything happens again,</b>

05:12.040 --> 05:15.080
<b>please send me a report.</b>

05:12.500 --> 05:15.080
"If anything happens again, please send me a report."

05:15.080 --> 05:16.920
She's deeply into her big bro.

05:16.920 --> 05:18.250
Uh... Yeah...

05:18.460 --> 05:19.580
That bad?

05:20.000 --> 05:21.830
Whoa! Another message came in.

05:21.830 --> 05:22.330
Oh...!

05:22.330 --> 05:24.330
<b>You have a new message.</b>

05:22.580 --> 05:24.130
Oh... It's Big Sis.

05:24.330 --> 05:27.330
<b>Don't need you today.</b>

05:24.960 --> 05:27.330
You know, Sajo, your fam's kind of matter of fact...

05:27.630 --> 05:30.830
Well, plus, she's not the meddling type from the get-go.

05:31.000 --> 05:33.580
Speaking of, I haven't seen her since the weekend.

05:33.580 --> 05:34.330
What's up with that?

05:34.830 --> 05:36.040
You two fighting or something?

05:36.040 --> 05:40.000
Nope. Well, it is unusual we haven't
spoken for this long, though.

05:38.460 --> 05:39.000
<b>Understood.</b>

05:39.330 --> 05:41.080
<b>Understood.</b>

05:49.290 --> 05:49.830
<b>Anpan</b>

05:50.210 --> 05:51.710
Sajo!

05:51.710 --> 05:54.880
Whoa! A feral Yamazaki has come jumping out.

05:55.040 --> 05:56.290
What's up with that!?

05:56.290 --> 05:58.210
You're hyper, as usual.

05:58.210 --> 06:00.040
No, I'm like super unexcited.

06:00.330 --> 06:05.710
You know, moving to new seats is cruel.
But, well, it's nice that I've gotten to know Koga.   

06:05.710 --> 06:07.130
Huh? Koga is-

06:09.420 --> 06:11.880
I'm gonna do it with my new boyfriend soon!

06:13.080 --> 06:15.880
Seriously? Were you two acquainted with each other?

06:16.170 --> 06:17.880
We're connected through Murata.

06:18.000 --> 06:19.710
Ah. From women's basketball.

06:20.290 --> 06:23.250
If you're going so far as to be all alone eating
by yourself, then you wanna eat together?   

06:23.250 --> 06:25.000
Hey, this dude's gonna join too!

06:25.210 --> 06:26.750
Huh!? Hey! I-

06:26.920 --> 06:30.460
Oh, it's you, Sajo! What? You wanna mingle with us too?

06:30.710 --> 06:32.040
Uh, yeah...

06:32.500 --> 06:35.210
You know, you've been quiet lately.
You being an introvert?

06:35.210 --> 06:38.460
Introvert. Yeah, I'm an introvert. Look at where my seat is.

06:38.460 --> 06:39.040
Huh?

06:39.040 --> 06:41.830
The very front! In the corner! That's hilarious!  

06:41.830 --> 06:43.290
That does crack me up!

06:43.710 --> 06:45.380
I don't get it, but I guess it was funny...

06:45.790 --> 06:48.380
Anyway, what's going on with you and Natsukawa-chan?

06:48.380 --> 06:50.670
You know, we haven't seen the "martial squabbles" lately.

06:50.880 --> 06:53.420
"Yamazaki, how dare you take her from me."

06:53.420 --> 06:54.750
I haven't taken her!

06:54.750 --> 06:56.380
Or rather, have you two done it already?

06:56.380 --> 06:57.040
Gross!

06:57.460 --> 07:01.170
You two have been in that kind of relationship since
middle school, right? You two do it? Have ya?  

07:01.290 --> 07:03.420
Don't be stupid. I don't even know where her house is.

07:03.420 --> 07:05.460
What's up with that!? You fail as a husband.

07:05.460 --> 07:07.380
Maybe he's not attractive to her?

07:07.380 --> 07:10.960
Well, you know, Sajo is in
many ways ordinary. Like his face.

07:10.960 --> 07:11.540
Huh!?

07:11.670 --> 07:14.960
In the time that we hadn't talked in a while,
you've gotten carried away with yourself.

07:15.130 --> 07:17.250
Speaking of, Yamazaki, what about you?

07:17.330 --> 07:20.920
Well, of course, I've been popular with the girls!
Plus, I've been like asked out too!  

07:21.040 --> 07:22.580
Uh-huh. Who?

07:22.790 --> 07:26.210
Don't freak out when you hear this, okay?
It's Okumura from Class A.

07:26.290 --> 07:27.080
That's hilarious!  

07:27.330 --> 07:29.460
Although I think she's definitely not serious about it!

07:29.460 --> 07:30.080
Oh...

07:31.040 --> 07:33.460
Yamazaki, hey, c'mon, please talk to me.

07:33.460 --> 07:35.540
Come to think of it, Sajo, what about the girl from before?

07:35.540 --> 07:36.830
What? "From before"?

07:37.080 --> 07:39.580
That brown-haired girl! You two did it, right!?

07:39.710 --> 07:43.250
Oh, you mean Aizawa?
You guys are misunderstanding that.

07:43.460 --> 07:47.460
Despite how she looks, Aizawa has been devoted to
that senpai since the time she enrolled here, so-

07:47.460 --> 07:48.250
Wataru!

07:48.250 --> 07:48.830
Huh?

07:49.330 --> 07:51.880
What? I was just about to give
an important back-up for Aizawa and...

07:51.880 --> 07:52.830
Come here!

07:53.250 --> 07:53.830
Hey!

07:53.830 --> 07:55.330
Don't grab me suddenly-

07:55.330 --> 07:55.960
Whoa!

07:55.960 --> 07:57.540
That's hilarious, for sure!  

07:57.670 --> 07:58.790
Whoa! What the hell!?

07:59.380 --> 08:01.880
<b>Music Room</b>

08:05.790 --> 08:08.040
Why is she this angry?

08:08.750 --> 08:09.960
N-Natsukawa.

08:10.330 --> 08:11.790
Wh-what!?

08:12.080 --> 08:14.670
You're angry about something right? Um...

08:14.960 --> 08:16.670
H-hang on, just a sec, okay?

08:17.040 --> 08:21.170
Um... The reason why Natsukawa is angry is...?

08:23.710 --> 08:27.500
There are way too many things that ring a bell!

08:31.420 --> 08:32.130
Ugh!

08:36.920 --> 08:40.960
<b>The Dreaming Boy</b>

08:36.920 --> 08:40.960
<b>is a Realist</b>

08:42.210 --> 08:44.710
C-calm down, okay? Natsukawa.

08:45.170 --> 08:47.210
And calm down, me!

08:47.580 --> 08:49.580
Let's just back off a little. Okay?

08:49.580 --> 08:50.330
Oh!

08:50.790 --> 08:54.670
I know. Would you please give me a hint about
the number one thing that is irritating you?

08:55.040 --> 08:57.330
I don't even know from what
I should start apologizing for-

08:57.500 --> 08:59.920
You... Because...

09:00.250 --> 09:02.080
Huh? I, what?

09:02.880 --> 09:05.710
Because you were talking to those girls...

09:06.420 --> 09:07.540
What?

09:08.080 --> 09:12.460
"Those girls," as in from just now, like Koga
and her corps from a different dimension?

09:15.080 --> 09:15.830
Yeah...

09:16.040 --> 09:17.330
Does that mean...

09:18.960 --> 09:22.710
H-hey! Don't take it the wrong way! It's not like that!

09:22.710 --> 09:25.630
I know that! That's why I don't understand!

09:25.630 --> 09:27.040
I-I mean...

09:28.250 --> 09:29.460
Oh, never mind!

09:29.460 --> 09:31.250
Hey wait! Natsukawa!

09:34.330 --> 09:37.000
What is up with that? How is she that cute...?

09:41.710 --> 09:44.040
I don't get it. I totally don't get it...

09:44.500 --> 09:45.830
Tap, tap!

09:46.330 --> 09:49.040
What's wrong, Sajotchi? You're making a weird face.

09:49.040 --> 09:50.880
You know a weird face is the usual.

09:51.000 --> 09:52.170
That's true, but...

09:52.170 --> 09:53.380
Deny that, will ya?

09:53.880 --> 09:58.880
Hey. Would Natsukawa get angry if I was talking
to like Yamazaki or Koga and the others?

09:58.880 --> 10:02.750
Oh? And why do you think Aichi would get angry over
that?

10:02.830 --> 10:07.290
That's what I want to know! Aw, jeez! What the hell!

10:09.210 --> 10:11.920
No, calm down. Don't take it literally.

10:12.500 --> 10:14.830
Natsukawa didn't say it with that kind of intention.   

10:15.420 --> 10:18.790
Then what was she intending, when she said
such a pathetically adorable thing?

10:19.330 --> 10:21.710
She's so cute I want to hug her tight.

10:21.710 --> 10:24.460
You know, your true intentions are leaking out.
Not that you could do that anyway.

10:24.460 --> 10:28.420
Well, of course. There's no way I'd be allowed
to do something like that to Natsukawa.

10:28.580 --> 10:29.920
Yeah, yeah...

10:30.420 --> 10:31.170
Oh!

10:31.580 --> 10:33.000
Why? Hey, look!

10:33.000 --> 10:33.960
Hey!

10:33.960 --> 10:34.880
What!?

10:36.330 --> 10:37.000
Oh!

10:37.460 --> 10:38.670
I won't take up your time.

10:39.630 --> 10:40.960
Can you step out for just a little bit?

10:41.920 --> 10:45.210
I don't mind if it's leisurely.
All I have to do is go home after this.

10:47.670 --> 10:48.420
Kei...

10:48.420 --> 10:50.040
Huh? Aichi.

10:51.380 --> 10:52.420
Um, so...

10:53.710 --> 10:56.710
<b>Student Council Room</b>

10:54.080 --> 10:55.540
Sorry this is out of the blue.

10:55.830 --> 10:56.710
Not at all.

10:57.080 --> 10:58.920
Did you want to talk about me helping out again?

10:59.210 --> 11:01.750
That would help, but this time that isn't it.

11:02.210 --> 11:02.920
Okay...

11:03.500 --> 11:06.500
Wataru. How do you think of yourself?

11:06.920 --> 11:09.790
Excuse me? As in, me personally?  

11:10.040 --> 11:12.420
That's right. I'd like to hear your self-evaluation.

11:12.960 --> 11:16.500
I think I'm an ordinary guy. I'm just a commoner.

11:17.000 --> 11:17.880
I see...

11:19.790 --> 11:23.580
I hear you had a crush on one girl for many years.  

11:23.580 --> 11:25.460
What!? How did you know...?

11:25.830 --> 11:27.130
Why did you stop?

11:27.790 --> 11:29.710
There is no reason for me to speak of that.

11:31.170 --> 11:32.380
Well, that's true too.

11:33.580 --> 11:36.500
In any case, something has changed about you recently.

11:37.040 --> 11:38.830
Well, that's... Yes.

11:39.500 --> 11:43.290
Rather than change, I think it's more that
I have stopped doing things that are uncalled for.

11:43.670 --> 11:47.380
I see. I won't ask the reason for that, but...

11:47.710 --> 11:49.130
Does Kaede know?

11:49.130 --> 11:51.460
Big Sis? Why would she?

11:51.830 --> 11:54.420
Based on your reaction,
it doesn't seem like you've told her.

11:54.420 --> 11:57.670
Big Sis is the person who has the least interest
in me, in the whole world, you know?

11:58.000 --> 11:59.830
There is no need for me to talk to her.

12:00.210 --> 12:01.250
That's unbelievable.

12:01.540 --> 12:02.250
Huh?

12:02.670 --> 12:05.500
The truth is, Kaede is bewildered by your change.

12:05.750 --> 12:08.710
No, nope. This is the person who
would say something cold-blooded,  

12:08.710 --> 12:13.380
while ordering me to go buy something like
Haagen-Dazs, you know? For that Big Sis to-  

12:13.380 --> 12:14.830
And I'm saying that big sister of yours.

12:16.330 --> 12:19.170
Um, I'm kind of not understanding
what you are getting at.

12:19.540 --> 12:23.460
Kaede thinks that she herself
is the cause of your change.

12:23.790 --> 12:27.330
She said she might have destroyed
her little brother's precious springtime of life.

12:28.750 --> 12:30.670
Huh? What is up with that?

12:30.960 --> 12:34.540
Wataru. Were you not told by Kaede,
ever since you were little,

12:34.540 --> 12:38.750
that "you're just that level of a person",
or something like that?

12:38.920 --> 12:49.170
<b>Student</b>

12:38.920 --> 12:49.170
<b>Council</b>

12:39.330 --> 12:40.170
Yeah...

12:40.580 --> 12:45.170
I've had an inkling that Kaede has something
like feelings of guilt towards you.

12:45.630 --> 12:49.000
We also did cheer her up by saying
that that's not the case, but...

12:49.460 --> 12:53.040
This is the first time we've seen Kaede
weak heartedly whine about something.

12:53.040 --> 12:55.250
Huh? That Big Sis?

12:56.080 --> 12:58.170
You know, there's no need for me to lie here.

12:58.960 --> 12:59.670
Oh...

13:01.710 --> 13:02.960
You're serious?

13:03.290 --> 13:07.250
I understand. As this is about one's own relative,
I'll do something about it.

13:07.580 --> 13:10.330
I appreciate it. A place has been arranged.

13:10.630 --> 13:14.170
What? That's not really... Something like
a family meeting can be discussed at home-

13:15.500 --> 13:16.210
Uh...

13:20.040 --> 13:22.710
Senpai, please let me ask you just one thing.

13:23.040 --> 13:23.830
What's that?

13:24.250 --> 13:28.750
Senpai, did you bring up this topic because
you don't want Big Sis to be sad?

13:29.500 --> 13:33.880
Or is it because you're irritated at me
for being the cause of Big Sis's distress?

13:34.380 --> 13:35.080
Yeah.

13:35.080 --> 13:36.130
It's both.

13:36.750 --> 13:38.880
Are you worried about whether
you'll be able to talk about it properly?

13:39.130 --> 13:45.580
No. Given that Big Sis is habitually strong-willed,
I don't think she'll do something like admit it honestly.

13:45.580 --> 13:46.380
Yeah...

13:46.580 --> 13:51.500
But that's not to say that I intend to be like usual
and bow down and cater to her either...   

13:58.330 --> 14:01.210
Senpai, you understand how
good-looking you are, don't you?

14:01.670 --> 14:04.000
I got carried away with that and
went through a bitter experience.

14:04.380 --> 14:08.580
The one who picked me up and rescued me,
from the point I'd tumbled down to, was your big sister.

14:08.580 --> 14:09.670
Are you serious?

14:10.540 --> 14:12.250
Well, I'm counting on you!

14:12.750 --> 14:14.170
Oh!

14:17.130 --> 14:19.040
You know, this is just too sudden...

14:20.500 --> 14:23.540
So, that means Big Sis was
avoiding me on purpose, huh...?

14:24.960 --> 14:25.790
Oh!

14:29.830 --> 14:32.250
I don't want to see my own
family member's dejected face.

14:33.040 --> 14:37.000
Even if it belongs to the audacious
and self-indulgent Big Sis...

14:48.080 --> 14:48.920
Big Sis.

14:53.670 --> 14:56.960
<b>Student</b>

14:53.670 --> 14:56.960
<b>Council</b>

14:57.170 --> 14:59.460
Huh? Why are you here...?

14:59.710 --> 15:03.420
You know, I wouldn't come to a place like this
if I wasn't summoned. And you, Big Sis?

15:03.710 --> 15:05.330
Rin said she'll come later.

15:05.330 --> 15:06.250
Rin?

15:06.830 --> 15:10.880
Oh, I don't think Morals and Discipline
Committee Chair Shinomiya-sama will be coming.

15:11.170 --> 15:13.790
Why? But that's what Renji told me.

15:14.130 --> 15:20.250
Well, that's Hanawa-senpai's little white lie.
So, Big Sis, I hear you're depressed about something?

15:20.460 --> 15:21.880
Huh!? What!?

15:22.210 --> 15:26.290
A very loose-tongued Student Council
President let it slip to me.

15:26.710 --> 15:30.000
He probably didn't feel good
about leaving things as is, after all.

15:30.000 --> 15:32.960
W-wait, hang on! That's not it!

15:32.960 --> 15:36.380
Hey, Big Sis. Say ten good traits about me.

15:36.540 --> 15:38.420
What!? What're you suddenly-

15:38.420 --> 15:40.500
If you're at the point of being depressed,
you won't be able to say them.

15:40.500 --> 15:42.830
What!? Why, you...!

15:43.290 --> 15:44.670
Okay, within ten seconds.

15:45.040 --> 15:48.960
10, 9, 8, 7.

15:47.080 --> 15:48.960
Wh-what!? Good traits...

15:48.960 --> 15:53.330
U-um... Good traits, good traits, good traits.
Your good traits?

15:49.250 --> 15:51.380
6, 5...

15:53.790 --> 15:57.540
It's fine. Okay, next. Ten ordinary traits about me.

15:57.790 --> 15:58.830
F-face!

15:59.420 --> 16:00.330
"Face"...?

16:00.330 --> 16:03.710
Height! Personality! Body type!
Intelligence! Financial power!

16:03.830 --> 16:04.710
"Financial power"?

16:04.710 --> 16:08.960
Hairstyle! Fashion sense! Physical strength!
Cleanliness! Body odor! Interestingness!

16:08.960 --> 16:10.500
How good you are at being a little brother! And-  

16:10.500 --> 16:12.830
Ten traits! You've already said ten things!

16:17.130 --> 16:20.210
See? I knew it. Big Sis, those are your true feelings.

16:20.830 --> 16:23.170
You think I'm an ordinary guy.

16:23.170 --> 16:25.170
Y-you're wrong! That's not...

16:25.330 --> 16:28.460
Big Sis, all you did was teach me
the truth about reality, right?

16:29.040 --> 16:31.380
Why are you worrying when that's so unlike you?

16:31.710 --> 16:32.460
Oh...

16:33.710 --> 16:36.830
It's true that recently I've given up
as hopeless on various things.

16:37.250 --> 16:42.170
But that's something I got passionate about
by choice and then cooled off on, by choice.  

16:43.130 --> 16:45.670
So, Big Sis, there's no reason for you
to say a lot of things about that.

16:46.000 --> 16:46.830
Uh...

16:49.040 --> 16:50.750
Well, so it's like that.

16:51.540 --> 16:53.830
Something like this happened before...

16:54.080 --> 16:54.750
Huh?

16:55.290 --> 17:00.290
Outwardly, they said they gave up on the person
they liked, but the truth was they couldn't give up.

17:00.790 --> 17:03.170
And by doing so, there was
a person who had a breakdown.

17:03.380 --> 17:06.420
That's why I thought you might end up the same way too.

17:07.130 --> 17:08.290
What's up with that?

17:08.290 --> 17:13.290
If that was the case, then the one
who made you do that might be me.

17:13.750 --> 17:18.290
So, I'm a wimpy guy who totally
can't forget about Natsukawa?

17:22.000 --> 17:26.960
I did say disparaging things about you,
but I wasn't serious, so have confidence in yourself.

17:27.580 --> 17:30.830
Giving up on a girl you've loved for years is a shame.

17:32.170 --> 17:32.830
Huh?

17:32.830 --> 17:39.710
So, I'll be careful, okay? I won't make fun of you anymore
and I won't say unreasonable things.

17:40.080 --> 17:43.710
So, there's no need for you to be
so self-deprecating anymore-

17:44.080 --> 17:45.420
That's enough.

17:45.710 --> 17:46.380
What...!?

17:47.080 --> 17:50.540
"I'll be careful..."? And that's supposed
to make me get confidence?

17:50.790 --> 17:51.880
I didn't mean it like that...!

17:51.880 --> 17:53.920
Is that your idea of having felt regret?

17:54.670 --> 17:57.460
Are you trying to become a kind big sister
at this point or something?

17:58.330 --> 18:02.790
You know, I've never even once had something
like a kind and pretty older sister.

18:05.710 --> 18:08.580
It's true that I probably took a lot of flak from you.

18:09.250 --> 18:10.790
But you know, that's fine.

18:11.420 --> 18:12.790
Because we're siblings.

18:12.790 --> 18:13.830
Siblings...

18:14.210 --> 18:16.580
You make me run errands,
and you go without saying a word of thanks,

18:16.580 --> 18:19.670
as you lie sprawled out on the living room sofa
as if you own the place, and you complain,

18:19.670 --> 18:24.040
as you play with your smartphone, while you stuff
your mouth with a steamed pork bun, like a queen.  

18:24.540 --> 18:25.580
Oh...

18:26.080 --> 18:31.580
Big Sis, that's who you are, right?
If that's not it, then that person isn't my big sis at all.

18:31.830 --> 18:32.830
You...

18:33.080 --> 18:36.880
At the least, that shitty big sis is the one I like best.

18:37.210 --> 18:38.330
What...!?

18:38.710 --> 18:42.830
That's why for you to do something like being
mindful at this point is just annoying, so stop it.  

18:45.210 --> 18:46.130
What?

18:49.830 --> 18:55.000
Are you sure that's okay? You know,
this is the last chance to have me be kind to you.

18:55.210 --> 18:58.290
Why is it the last? You should be kind in general.

18:58.290 --> 18:59.830
Huh!? Which do you-

19:00.380 --> 19:01.630
I said to hang on a sec!

19:01.630 --> 19:05.080
You! How dare you talk to your big sister like that!

19:05.210 --> 19:07.630
Huh!? What!? Natsukawa and Ashida!?

19:08.830 --> 19:09.580
Whoa!

19:09.580 --> 19:11.250
Hurry up and apologize!

19:11.250 --> 19:11.830
Uh...!

19:11.830 --> 19:15.250
You know your older sister would be sad
if you said those kinds of rude things!

19:16.080 --> 19:17.670
Hey! Aichi, stop it!

19:17.670 --> 19:19.540
You know, Sajotchi's gonna die!

19:19.540 --> 19:22.250
What's happening!? Hang on, were you two watching!?

19:19.540 --> 19:20.500
Why!?

19:22.330 --> 19:24.500
I think I might've said some rather embarrassing things.

19:24.750 --> 19:27.250
Don't worry! We only heard the last part!

19:27.420 --> 19:28.630
I can't trust that.

19:28.630 --> 19:29.710
Are you listening to me!?

19:30.210 --> 19:31.830
Now, now, Aichi.

19:31.830 --> 19:33.130
N-Natsukawa.

19:33.130 --> 19:34.000
What!?

19:34.000 --> 19:35.670
Why are you here of all places?

19:35.670 --> 19:38.580
You were being taken away by
a Student Council member and...

19:38.580 --> 19:40.500
And you went out of your way to go to the rooftop?

19:40.500 --> 19:42.500
Oh! That's...!

19:50.630 --> 19:55.540
What? That's true. Why did I do something
like act as if I'm following after him...?

19:56.290 --> 19:58.380
Oh, uh, that was...

19:58.630 --> 19:59.880
Just by coincidence!

19:59.880 --> 20:00.750
Aichi!

20:03.290 --> 20:04.790
I've been left behind again...

20:04.790 --> 20:05.580
Again?

20:09.040 --> 20:11.830
So, it's just that I had my head in the clouds, huh?

20:11.830 --> 20:12.500
Huh?

20:13.040 --> 20:15.380
It's nothing. Stupid Wataru.

20:15.750 --> 20:18.420
What's up with that? You're totally back to usual.

20:18.830 --> 20:19.630
Hmpf!

20:38.500 --> 20:40.830
Natsukawa was being weird today.

20:43.670 --> 20:44.670
No! Nope, nope!

20:45.210 --> 20:46.670
More importantly, right now...

20:50.130 --> 20:52.420
While I'm here, I guess I'll buy that too and head home.

20:57.080 --> 20:57.830
Oh...

20:59.170 --> 21:00.210
What are you doing?

21:00.670 --> 21:02.250
You should at least say, "I'm home."

21:02.250 --> 21:03.670
Yeah. I'm home.

21:07.040 --> 21:08.580
Sorry about that, Big Sis.

21:08.580 --> 21:09.250
Huh?

21:09.420 --> 21:11.130
For saying rude things.

21:11.290 --> 21:13.000
Huh!? You...

21:13.540 --> 21:14.130
Oh!

21:17.540 --> 21:18.880
N-not right now.

21:18.880 --> 21:21.580
Uh-huh. Then I'll eat these myself.

21:22.540 --> 21:24.460
I-I didn't say that I didn't want any!

21:24.670 --> 21:26.330
You know they don't taste good after they get cold.

21:26.330 --> 21:27.500
Then I'll eat them now!

21:27.630 --> 21:29.000
Oh! Hey!

21:32.420 --> 21:35.250
Huh!? I can't tell what you're saying!

21:35.630 --> 21:37.630
Give 'em back! C'mon! Give them back!

21:37.960 --> 21:39.960
Oh! Hey! Don't eat them!

21:40.420 --> 21:42.290
Dammit! If it's come to this...!  

21:42.540 --> 21:43.170
Huh!?

21:43.500 --> 21:47.790
(What're ya doing!? Stop that!
Don't photograph me like this!)

21:48.250 --> 21:49.380
Alright!

21:49.790 --> 21:55.170
I bet those good-looking guys of the Student Council
don't know about Big Sis' unguarded looks like this.

21:57.290 --> 21:59.500
If something happens to me, I'll sell these...

21:59.750 --> 22:00.580
Huh?

22:02.170 --> 22:04.420
Uh-oh! Oh no!

22:05.880 --> 22:07.880
Take that! You stupid Wataru!

22:28.460 --> 22:30.920
So annoying! Or so it seems, right?

22:31.210 --> 22:34.500
Aw! I wish I hadn't said that...

22:35.330 --> 22:41.460
But you know, why're you suddenly making
that curt face towards me...?

22:43.170 --> 22:45.380
A text that's been left on read and abandoned

22:45.380 --> 22:47.670
But there are replies if it’s a group text, kind of thing

22:47.880 --> 22:49.830
I thought we were close, but then you became distant

22:50.080 --> 22:51.630
Why am I this lonely?

22:51.630 --> 22:53.500
You're not going to chase after me, today?

22:53.500 --> 22:55.040
I wish I could be honest with myself

22:56.500 --> 23:02.830
That's because it's the first time
I learned there's such a heartrending feeling...

23:02.830 --> 23:04.250
And yet, hey!

23:04.250 --> 23:05.790
Why're you going away??

23:05.790 --> 23:07.540
Why is it a secret!?

23:07.750 --> 23:09.920
I'm full of frustration and...

23:09.920 --> 23:11.290
Oh! Oh!

23:11.290 --> 23:13.000
I can't say something like this

23:13.000 --> 23:17.000
But earlier those weren't my true feelings

23:17.000 --> 23:18.380
Let that get through to you

23:18.460 --> 23:20.080
Why do I get angry...?

23:20.080 --> 23:21.630
I can't be cute...

23:21.630 --> 23:24.080
You don't like me anymore...??

23:24.250 --> 23:26.960
Oh! Oh! Oh, oh!

23:28.960 --> 23:29.920
Why?

23:30.580 --> 23:31.880
Don't hate me

23:34.920 --> 23:36.290
...Listen, "You see...!"
